IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cc-dates`

-- County Court Act 1958 (Vic) -- the rules a party to a civil proceeding meets: jurisdiction (Part II), settling a child's
-- injury claim and money for children and persons under disability (ss 39A-39C), arbitration and mediation (Part II
-- Division 6), trial (Part V), judgment, interest, appeal and transfer of judgment (Part VI, ss 17V, 86), costs and fees
-- (ss 33, 34, 79A(6)), and the employee whose earnings are attached (s 49A(3)).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in cc-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule. Nothing
-- here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("does not have jurisdiction",
-- "shall not be allowed", "must not be made unless", "does not apply so as to authorize", "neither party shall be liable",
-- "no appeal shall lie", "no such certificate shall be granted", "unless", an "if", "where", "when" or "provided that"
-- condition that fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The
-- Court's and the registrar's judgments ("satisfied", "thinks fit", "in the opinion of", leave, consent) are inputs: the
-- answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Forks (Fn) are listed in NOTES.md.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the County Court
-- Act 1958, Version No. 186 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `County Court Act 1958 -- the rules for a party to a civil proceeding`

§§ `Answers that combine`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a no` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST v THEN (NOT v)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a yes` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST v THEN v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- Two answers that must both be yes: a no from either is a no; yes only if both are yes; otherwise not answered.
GIVEN `the first` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `the second` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both of` `the first` `and also` `the second` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `is a no` `the first` OR `is a no` `the second` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `is a yes` `the first` AND `is a yes` `the second` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part II Division 2 -- civil jurisdiction (ss 36, 37, 39, 51, 55)`

-- s 37(1): "The court has jurisdiction to hear and determine -- (a) all applications, claims, disputes and civil proceedings
-- regardless of the type of relief sought or the subject-matter as are not by this or any other Act excluded from its
-- jurisdiction; and (b) all civil proceedings against municipal councils in respect of loss or injury sustained by persons
-- or property by reason of accidents, upon or while using any highway, street, road, bridge, ferry or jetty or upon or in or
-- while using any paths or any land or building under the control of a municipal council; and (c) all other civil
-- proceedings in respect of which jurisdiction is given to the court by this or any other Act."
-- s 37(2): "The court does not have jurisdiction to hear or determine any application, claim, dispute or other civil
-- proceeding (other than proceedings to which subsection (1)(b) or (c) applies) -- ... (c) brought by application for a
-- prerogative writ or an order in the nature of a prerogative writ; or (d) brought upon a judgment of the Supreme Court."
-- There is no money limit: the "jurisdictional limit" (s 3(1)) and s 38 were repealed by No. 50/2006.
DECLARE `Kind of civil proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a claim of any other kind`
    `a claim against a municipal council for an accident on a road or other place it controls`
    `a proceeding another Act gives the County Court jurisdiction over`
    `an application for a prerogative writ or an order in the nature of one`
    `a proceeding brought upon a judgment of the Supreme Court`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of civil proceeding`
      `another Act excludes it from the County Court's jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 -- the County Court has jurisdiction over the kind of proceeding` `the kind` `another Act excludes it from the County Court's jurisdiction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an application for a prerogative writ or an order in the nature of one` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a proceeding brought upon a judgment of the Supreme Court` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a claim against a municipal council for an accident on a road or other place it controls` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding another Act gives the County Court jurisdiction over` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a claim of any other kind` THEN
        IF `another Act excludes it from the County Court's jurisdiction`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 37(1)(a) grants only what is "not ... excluded"; the excluding Act answers, fork F1)
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 36: "The court shall have power to hear and determine every proceeding in respect of which jurisdiction is conferred upon
-- it by this or any other Act, notwithstanding that part of the cause of action arose outside Victoria, provided that a
-- material part of the cause of action arose within Victoria, and shall have power to hear and determine every such
-- proceeding notwithstanding that the whole cause of action arose outside Victoria, provided that the defendant or accused
-- resided within Victoria at the time of the service of the originating process upon such defendant or accused."
DECLARE `Where the cause of action arose` IS ONE OF
    `wholly within Victoria`
    `partly outside Victoria, with a material part within Victoria`
    `partly outside Victoria, with no material part within Victoria`
    `wholly outside Victoria`

GIVEN `where it arose` IS A `Where the cause of action arose`
      `the defendant resided in Victoria when served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- where the cause of action arose is no bar` `where it arose` `the defendant resided in Victoria when served` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where it arose`
    WHEN `wholly within Victoria` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `partly outside Victoria, with a material part within Victoria` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `partly outside Victoria, with no material part within Victoria` THEN
        IF `the defendant resided in Victoria when served`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the first proviso fails and the second speaks only of "the whole cause of action" arising outside Victoria; fork F2)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `wholly outside Victoria` THEN
        IF `the defendant resided in Victoria when served` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 37(3): "If a verdict is returned for or a judgment is given for an amount greater than the amount sought to be recovered
-- in the civil proceeding by the plaintiff -- (a) the court must find and record the amount of the verdict or judgment; and
-- (b) the plaintiff may recover the full amount of the verdict or judgment or, if the full amount is liable to be reduced in
-- accordance with Part V of the Wrongs Act 1958, the amount to which the full amount is so liable to be reduced, even if that
-- full amount or reduced amount is greater than the amount sought to be recovered."
-- Part V of the Wrongs Act 1958 is contributory negligence: the reduction is the court's ("just and equitable"), asked as a
-- percentage.
GIVEN `the verdict or judgment` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount I sought` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage reduction for my contributory negligence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 37(3) -- what I may recover above the amount I sought` `the verdict or judgment` `the amount I sought` `the percentage reduction for my contributory negligence` MEANS
    IF `the verdict or judgment` GREATER THAN `the amount I sought`
    THEN JUST (`the verdict or judgment` TIMES (100 MINUS `the percentage reduction for my contributory negligence`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 37(3) speaks only of a verdict greater than the amount sought)

-- s 39(2): "If a civil proceeding is wholly or partly beyond the jurisdiction of the court, the court may -- (a) amend the
-- originating process for the purpose of bringing the proceeding within jurisdiction; or (b) order that the proceeding be
-- stayed pending the making of an application under Part 3 of the Courts (Case Transfer) Act 1991; or (c) order that the
-- proceeding be struck out and award costs as if the court had jurisdiction and the proceeding were dismissed."
-- s 55: "Whenever an action or matter is commenced over which the court has no jurisdiction, the judge or associate judge
-- ... shall, unless the parties consent to the court having jurisdiction, order it to be struck out, and shall have power to
-- award costs ... as if the court had jurisdiction there and the plaintiff had not appeared or had appeared and failed to
-- prove his demand or complaint." The two overlap for a proceeding wholly beyond jurisdiction (finding 2, fork F3).
DECLARE `How far the proceeding is beyond jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `within jurisdiction`
    `partly beyond jurisdiction`
    `wholly beyond jurisdiction`

DECLARE `What becomes of a proceeding beyond jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: the proceeding is within jurisdiction`
    `it may go on with the parties' consent to the Court having jurisdiction (s 55)`
    `the Court may amend it, stay it for a transfer application, or strike it out with costs as if it were dismissed (s 39(2))`
    `it must be struck out with costs as if the plaintiff failed, unless the Court first amends it or stays it for a transfer (ss 55, 39(2))`

GIVEN `how far` IS A `How far the proceeding is beyond jurisdiction`
      `the parties consent to the Court having jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of a proceeding beyond jurisdiction`
`ss 39(2), 55 -- what becomes of a proceeding beyond jurisdiction` `how far` `the parties consent to the Court having jurisdiction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how far`
    WHEN `within jurisdiction` THEN `nothing: the proceeding is within jurisdiction`
    WHEN `partly beyond jurisdiction` THEN `the Court may amend it, stay it for a transfer application, or strike it out with costs as if it were dismissed (s 39(2))`
    WHEN `wholly beyond jurisdiction` THEN
        IF `the parties consent to the Court having jurisdiction`
        THEN `it may go on with the parties' consent to the Court having jurisdiction (s 55)`
        ELSE `it must be struck out with costs as if the plaintiff failed, unless the Court first amends it or stays it for a transfer (ss 55, 39(2))`

-- s 51(1): a defence or counter-claim beyond jurisdiction "shall not affect the competence or the duty of the court to
-- dispose of the whole matter in controversy so far as relates to the demand of the plaintiff and the defence thereto, but no
-- relief exceeding that which the court has jurisdiction to administer shall be given to the defendant upon any such
-- counter-claim unless the parties or their respective legal practitioners have consented in writing to the court hearing
-- and determining the counter-claim."
GIVEN `the counter-claim involves matter beyond the Court's jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties consented in writing to the Court hearing the counter-claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51 -- relief beyond jurisdiction may be given on the counter-claim` `the counter-claim involves matter beyond the Court's jurisdiction` `the parties consented in writing to the Court hearing the counter-claim` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the counter-claim involves matter beyond the Court's jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 51 speaks only of a counter-claim beyond jurisdiction)
           IF `the parties consented in writing to the Court hearing the counter-claim` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II Divisions 2, 2A, 2B -- a child's injury claim and money for children and persons under disability (ss 39A, 39B, 39C)`

-- s 39A(1): "If a minor is or appears to be entitled to recover damages for bodily injury (other than injury caused by or
-- arising out of the use of a motor car within the meaning of the Transport Accident Act 1986) and any parent or guardian or
-- next friend of the minor or any person standing in loco parentis to the minor or the State Trust (as the case may be)
-- believes that the amount of compensation in respect of the bodily injury offered or tendered by or on behalf of the person
-- or body from whom or which the damages are claimed is reasonable and adequate having regard to -- (a) the bodily injury
-- sustained; and (b) the probability or otherwise of the minor succeeding in any proceeding ... -- the parent or guardian or
-- next friend or person standing in loco parentis or the State Trust (as the case may be) is entitled in the name and on
-- behalf of the minor to enter into an agreement in writing ... to accept the amount of compensation so offered or tendered."
-- s 39A(10): "Nothing in this section applies in any case where a proceeding has been commenced in a court by or on behalf
-- of the minor for the recovery of damages for bodily injury."
-- "minor" is borrowed (Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 s 38: under 18), asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Who acts for the child` IS ONE OF
    `a parent`
    `a guardian`
    `a next friend`
    `a person standing in loco parentis`
    `the State Trust`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who acts for the child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39A(1) names` `who` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the child is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is or appears to be entitled to damages for bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury arose out of the use of a motor car` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who` IS A `Who acts for the child`
      `I believe the offer reasonable and adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proceeding for the damages has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(1), (10) -- I may agree for the child to accept the offer` `the child is a minor` `the child is or appears to be entitled to damages for bodily injury` `the injury arose out of the use of a motor car` `who` `I believe the offer reasonable and adequate` `a proceeding for the damages has been commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a proceeding for the damages has been commenced` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `the child is a minor` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `the child is or appears to be entitled to damages for bodily injury` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the injury arose out of the use of a motor car` THEN JUST FALSE -- fork F4: "(other than ...)" read as part of the "if"
           IF NOT (`s 39A(1) names` `who`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `I believe the offer reasonable and adequate` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 39A(4): "An agreement entered into in accordance with subsection (1) does not have any force or effect until it has been
-- filed and approved by order of the County Court in accordance with this section". An "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05,
-- (d)): JUST TRUE (still without force) before both, JUST FALSE after; never a claim that the agreement has force.
GIVEN `the agreement has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the County Court has approved it by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(4) -- the agreement is still without force` `the agreement has been filed` `the County Court has approved it by order` MEANS
    IF `the agreement has been filed` AND `the County Court has approved it by order`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 39A(2)(b): a filed agreement "must be accompanied by an affidavit made by the [person] who entered into the agreement
-- verifying the facts on which the agreement is based". s 39A(6): "An order under this section must not be made unless the
-- court is satisfied with respect to -- (a) the right of the parent, guardian, next friend or other person standing in loco
-- parentis or of the State Trust to act for the minor; and (b) the reasonableness and adequacy in the circumstances of the
-- amount of compensation; and (c) the genuineness of the agreement."
GIVEN `the agreement is filed with the verifying affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied of my right to act for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the amount is reasonable and adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the agreement is genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(2), (6) -- the Court may approve the agreement` `the agreement is filed with the verifying affidavit` `the Court is satisfied of my right to act for the child` `the Court is satisfied the amount is reasonable and adequate` `the Court is satisfied the agreement is genuine` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the agreement is filed with the verifying affidavit` THEN JUST FALSE -- fork F5: approval is of a filed agreement (s 39A(3), (4))
           IF     `the Court is satisfied of my right to act for the child`
              AND `the Court is satisfied the amount is reasonable and adequate`
              AND `the Court is satisfied the agreement is genuine` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 39A(8): "When an order approving an agreement has been complied with by the person or body from whom or which the damages
-- are claimed, that person or body is released and discharged from all liability to the minor in respect of the bodily
-- injury." "When" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)): before compliance, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the Court approved the agreement by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payer has complied with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(8) -- the payer is released from the child's injury claim` `the Court approved the agreement by order` `the payer has complied with the order` MEANS
    IF `the Court approved the agreement by order` AND `the payer has complied with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 39B(1): "If in any civil proceedings before the court it is adjudged or ordered that money be paid to a child ... the
-- money -- (a) is to be paid into court; and (b) unless the court otherwise orders, is to be paid out to an administrator
-- specified by the court." s 39C(1): "person under disability means -- (a) a minor; or (b) a person who is incapable by reason
-- of injury, disease, senility, illness or physical or mental infirmity of managing his or her affairs in relation to the
-- proceeding." s 39C(3): "Unless the court orders otherwise, in any proceeding in the court in which it is adjudged or ordered
-- that money be paid for a person under disability, that money must be paid into the Supreme Court ... by payment to the
-- Senior Master of the Supreme Court to be held in that Court on behalf of the person under disability." s 39C(6): "Nothing
-- in this section affects the operation of section 39B". For a minor both sections speak (finding 3); the list gives both.
-- "child" is not defined in the Act; asked as a minor (fork F6).
DECLARE `Where money for a child or person under disability goes` IS ONE OF
    `into the County Court, then out to an administrator the Court specifies (s 39B(1))`
    `into the County Court, then as the Court otherwise orders (s 39B(1))`
    `into the Supreme Court, to the Senior Master, to be held for the person (s 39C(3))`
    `as the Court orders otherwise than into the Supreme Court (s 39C(3))`

GIVEN `the person is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39C(1) -- a person under disability` `the person is a minor` `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding` IF
    `the person is a minor` OR `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding`

GIVEN `the person is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Where money for a child or person under disability goes`
`ss 39B, 39C -- where the money awarded goes` `the person is a minor` `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding` `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39B` `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39C` MEANS
    `the s 39B part` `++` `the s 39C part`
    WHERE
        `the s 39B part` MEANS
            IF `the person is a minor`
            THEN IF `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39B`
                 THEN LIST `into the County Court, then as the Court otherwise orders (s 39B(1))`
                 ELSE LIST `into the County Court, then out to an administrator the Court specifies (s 39B(1))`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the s 39C part` MEANS
            IF `s 39C(1) -- a person under disability` `the person is a minor` `the person cannot manage their affairs in the proceeding`
            THEN IF `the Court ordered otherwise under s 39C`
                 THEN LIST `as the Court orders otherwise than into the Supreme Court (s 39C(3))`
                 ELSE LIST `into the Supreme Court, to the Senior Master, to be held for the person (s 39C(3))`
            ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `the first list` IS A LIST OF `Where money for a child or person under disability goes`
      `the second list` IS A LIST OF `Where money for a child or person under disability goes`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Where money for a child or person under disability goes`
`the first list` `++` `the second list` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first list`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the second list`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN x FOLLOWED BY (xs `++` `the second list`)

§§ `Part II Division 6 -- arbitration and mediation (ss 46, 47, 47A, 47B)`

-- s 46(2): the award of arbitrators to whom the Court referred the proceeding on the parties' agreement "shall unless set
-- aside be binding final and conclusive on both parties; ... and such reference shall not be revocable by either party
-- thereto except by leave of the court." s 46(4): the Court may "on application to it at the first sitting held after the
-- expiration of one week after the entry of such award, set aside any such award ... or may refer such award back".
-- s 47: where the parties agree in writing and the Court acts as arbitrator, "such award and the judgment thereon shall not be
-- subject to question or appeal in any court whatever." s 47A: the Court may refer to mediation or arbitration "Subject to and
-- in accordance with the rules or the Civil Procedure Act 2010" (neither deposited here).
DECLARE `How the dispute went to arbitration` IS ONE OF
    `the parties agreed and the Court referred it to arbitrators they named (s 46)`
    `the parties agreed in writing and the Court acted as arbitrator (s 47)`
    `the Court referred it under s 47A`

DECLARE `What the arbitration award is` IS ONE OF
    `binding, final and conclusive unless set aside; the Court may set it aside or refer it back on an application at the first sitting after one week from its entry (s 46(2), (4))`
    `not open to question or appeal in any court (s 47)`
    `not answered here: the rules and the Civil Procedure Act 2010 govern (s 47A)`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How the dispute went to arbitration`
GIVETH A `What the arbitration award is`
`ss 46, 47, 47A -- what the arbitration award is` `how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `the parties agreed and the Court referred it to arbitrators they named (s 46)` THEN `binding, final and conclusive unless set aside; the Court may set it aside or refer it back on an application at the first sitting after one week from its entry (s 46(2), (4))`
    WHEN `the parties agreed in writing and the Court acted as arbitrator (s 47)` THEN `not open to question or appeal in any court (s 47)`
    WHEN `the Court referred it under s 47A` THEN `not answered here: the rules and the Civil Procedure Act 2010 govern (s 47A)`

-- s 47B: "Where the Court refers a proceeding or any part of a proceeding to mediation, other than judicial resolution
-- conference, unless all the parties who attend the mediation otherwise agree in writing, no evidence shall be admitted at
-- the hearing of the proceeding of anything said or done by any person at the mediation."
DECLARE `Kind of mediation` IS ONE OF
    `a mediation the Court referred the proceeding to`
    `a judicial resolution conference`
    `a mediation the Court did not refer`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of mediation`
      `all the parties who attended agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47B -- evidence of the mediation may be admitted at the hearing` `the kind` `all the parties who attended agreed in writing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a mediation the Court referred the proceeding to` THEN
        IF `all the parties who attended agreed in writing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a judicial resolution conference` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: excepted from s 47B; the Civil Procedure Act 2010 governs)
    WHEN `a mediation the Court did not refer` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 47B speaks only of a mediation the Court refers)

§§ `Part II Division 1 and Part V -- hearing and trial (ss 36AA, 67, 68, 70, 73(3), (3A))`

-- s 36AA(1): "The court may determine any matter in any proceeding, or determine any proceeding, without an oral hearing and
-- entirely on the basis of written submissions and without the appearance of the parties -- (a) if the court is satisfied that
-- it is in the interests of justice to do so; and (b) whether or not the parties consent to the court doing so." (2): not a
-- criminal proceeding. (3): the matters the Court weighs (nature, fair hearing, chance of legal advice, consent).
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36AA -- my civil proceeding may be decided on the papers` `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 67(1): "In all civil proceedings where the amount claimed or the value of the subject-matter exceeds $5000 the plaintiff or
-- defendant and in civil proceedings brought for the recovery of unliquidated damages the judge may require a jury to try the
-- said proceeding." (2): notice to the registrar and the other party as the Rules direct (not deposited).
`s 67(1) -- the amount a party's jury requires more than` MEANS 5000

GIVEN `the amount claimed or the value of the subject-matter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) -- I may require a jury` `the amount claimed or the value of the subject-matter` MEANS
    IF `the amount claimed or the value of the subject-matter` GREATER THAN `s 67(1) -- the amount a party's jury requires more than`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 68(2): "When the judge of his own motion has required any civil proceeding to be tried by a jury, neither party shall be
-- liable to pay the jury fees." The fees themselves are set by the Rules or regulations (not deposited).
DECLARE `Who required the jury` IS ONE OF
    `I did`
    `the other party did`
    `the judge, of the judge's own motion`
    `the judge, on a party's application`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who required the jury`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) -- I may be liable for the jury fees` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the judge, of the judge's own motion` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: who pays jury fees otherwise is for the Rules and the costs order)

-- s 70: "(1) Subject to Part VI, where a jury has given a verdict, judgment must be entered in accordance with the verdict.
-- (2) Despite subsection (1), the judge ... may, before the jury has given a verdict, grant leave to a party to apply for
-- judgment other than in accordance with the verdict of the jury. (3) If leave is granted under subsection (2), judgment may be
-- entered other than in accordance with the verdict of the jury."
GIVEN `the jury has given a verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge gave leave before the verdict to apply for another judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70 -- judgment must follow the jury's verdict` `the jury has given a verdict` `the judge gave leave before the verdict to apply for another judgment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the jury has given a verdict` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 70 speaks of a verdict given)
           IF `the judge gave leave before the verdict to apply for another judgment` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 73(3): "The court may also in every case whatever, and as often as it thinks fit, order a new trial to be had upon such
-- terms as it thinks reasonable". (3A): "Subsection (3) does not apply so as to authorize the court to order a new trial in
-- civil proceedings in which a jury has given a verdict."
GIVEN `a jury gave the verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(3), (3A) -- the County Court may order a new trial` `a jury gave the verdict` MEANS
    IF `a jury gave the verdict` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part VI -- interest, appeal, rehearing (ss 17V, 47, 72, 73(4), 74, 75)`

-- s 73(4): "Every judgment debt shall carry interest at the rate for the time being fixed under section 2 of the Penalty
-- Interest Rates Act 1983 from the time the judgment is entered or the order made or, in the case of costs to be assessed,
-- from the assessment of those costs or such other day as the court orders". The rate is not deposited: asked. Simple
-- interest by the day over a 365-day year, the rate held for the whole period (fork F7).
GIVEN `the judgment debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate, percent a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day interest runs from` IS A DATE
      `the day interest runs to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 73(4) -- the interest on the judgment debt` `the judgment debt` `the rate, percent a year` `the day interest runs from` `the day interest runs to` MEANS
    IF `the days` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the judgment debt` TIMES `the rate, percent a year` TIMES `the days` DIVIDED BY 36500
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the days` MEANS `the days from` `the day interest runs from` `to` `the day interest runs to`

-- s 74(1): "any party to a civil proceeding who is dissatisfied with any judgment or order of the court constituted by a
-- judge other than an associate judge may appeal from the same to the Court of Appeal with leave of the Court of Appeal".
-- (6): "Nothing herein contained shall authorize any party to appeal against any decision of the court given upon any question
-- as to the value of any real or personal property for the purpose of determining the question of the jurisdiction of the
-- court under this Act nor to appeal against the decision of the court on the ground that the proceedings might or should have
-- been taken at any other place of sitting of the County Court." (7): "No appeal shall lie from any judgment or order of the
-- court, if before it is pronounced the parties agree, in writing signed by themselves or their practitioners, that it shall
-- be final." s 75: from an associate judge, to the Trial Division of the Supreme Court, with leave of the associate judge or
-- the Trial Division. s 17V(3), (4): from a judicial registrar, an appeal or review as the Rules provide, or if they do not, a
-- hearing de novo by a judge. s 47: no appeal from an award where the Court acted as arbitrator. s 77: no prerogative writ.
DECLARE `Who decided` IS ONE OF
    `a judge`
    `an associate judge`
    `a judicial registrar`
    `the Court acting as arbitrator by the parties' written agreement (s 47)`

DECLARE `Where an appeal goes` IS ONE OF
    `no appeal or question in any court (s 47)`
    `no appeal: the parties agreed in writing before it was pronounced that it would be final (s 74(7))`
    `no appeal on that ground (s 74(6))`
    `to the Court of Appeal, with the Court of Appeal's leave (s 74(1))`
    `to the Trial Division of the Supreme Court, with leave of the associate judge or of the Trial Division (s 75)`
    `an appeal or review as the County Court Rules provide (s 17V(1), (3))`
    `a hearing de novo by a judge of the County Court (s 17V(4))`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who decided`
      `the parties agreed in writing it would be final` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground is a property value for jurisdiction or the place of sitting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Rules provide for appeal or review from a judicial registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where an appeal goes`
`ss 17V, 47, 74, 75 -- where my appeal goes` `who` `the parties agreed in writing it would be final` `the only ground is a property value for jurisdiction or the place of sitting` `the Rules provide for appeal or review from a judicial registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the Court acting as arbitrator by the parties' written agreement (s 47)` THEN `no appeal or question in any court (s 47)`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH IF `the parties agreed in writing it would be final` THEN `no appeal: the parties agreed in writing before it was pronounced that it would be final (s 74(7))`
               IF `the only ground is a property value for jurisdiction or the place of sitting` THEN `no appeal on that ground (s 74(6))` -- fork F8: "herein" read as the whole Act
               OTHERWISE `the route for` `who`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the decider` IS A `Who decided`
        GIVETH A `Where an appeal goes`
        `the route for` `the decider` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the decider`
            WHEN `an associate judge` THEN `to the Trial Division of the Supreme Court, with leave of the associate judge or of the Trial Division (s 75)`
            WHEN `a judicial registrar` THEN
                IF `the Rules provide for appeal or review from a judicial registrar`
                THEN `an appeal or review as the County Court Rules provide (s 17V(1), (3))`
                ELSE `a hearing de novo by a judge of the County Court (s 17V(4))`
            OTHERWISE `to the Court of Appeal, with the Court of Appeal's leave (s 74(1))`

-- s 72(1): when a party has appealed to the Court of Appeal and a re-hearing has been directed before the Supreme Court
-- constituted by a Judge, "any of the parties thereto shall be entitled (if the case was in the County Court tried before a
-- jury or if the Court of Appeal at the time of directing the re-hearing so orders) if the party so desires to have such
-- re-hearing before the Supreme Court so constituted and a jury of six persons."
GIVEN `a re-hearing before a Supreme Court judge was directed on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case was tried before a jury in the County Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Appeal so ordered when directing the re-hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) -- I am entitled to a jury on the re-hearing` `a re-hearing before a Supreme Court judge was directed on appeal` `the case was tried before a jury in the County Court` `the Court of Appeal so ordered when directing the re-hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `a re-hearing before a Supreme Court judge was directed on appeal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 72 speaks of a re-hearing directed on appeal)
           IF `the case was tried before a jury in the County Court` OR `the Court of Appeal so ordered when directing the re-hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 72(2): "The plaintiff may have a jury by giving the prothonotary and the defendant a notice in writing to the effect that
-- he requires a jury when giving notice of trial and by paying the proper jury fees." (3): "The defendant may have a jury by
-- giving the prothonotary and the plaintiff within four days after receiving notice of trial notice in writing to the effect
-- that he requires a jury and by paying the proper jury fees."
-- The defendant's step is a regulative rule: DO the notice WITHIN 4 days, counted from the day notice of trial is received
-- as day 0 (Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 s 44: "after" excludes that day), so the fourth day after is the last.
-- It is a condition of a right, not a duty: the LEST is the loss of the jury as of right, not a wrong (fork F9).
DECLARE `Re-hearing party` IS ONE OF
    `the defendant`

DECLARE `Re-hearing act` IS ONE OF
    `give notice in writing requiring a jury`

`s 72(3) -- the days the defendant has` MEANS 4

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Re-hearing party` `Re-hearing act`
`s 72(3) -- the defendant's jury notice within four days` MEANS
    PARTY `the defendant`
    DO `give notice in writing requiring a jury`
    WITHIN `s 72(3) -- the days the defendant has`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the defendant` BECAUSE "no notice requiring a jury within four days after receiving notice of trial: no jury as of right on the re-hearing (s 72(3))"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened (as in the Accident Compensation Act 1985 and Supreme Court Act 1986
-- encodings). On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the notice was given,
-- FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether giving it today would still be in
-- time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the notice` IS ONE OF
    `given in time`
    `not given in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Re-hearing party` `Re-hearing act`
      `the notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time it was given` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the notice`
`what became of the notice under` `the rule` `given` `the notice has been given` `at` `the time it was given` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the notice has been given`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was given`), (EVENT `the defendant` `give notice in writing requiring a jury` `the time it was given`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `given in time`
         OTHERWISE `not given in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the defendant` `give notice in writing requiring a jury` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not given in time`

DECLARE `My side` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`
    `the defendant side`

DECLARE `Where my jury on the re-hearing stands` IS ONE OF
    `no jury as of right on the re-hearing (s 72(1))`
    `the jury notice is in time and the jury fees are paid: a jury of six (s 72)`
    `the jury notice is in time, but the jury fees are still to be paid (s 72(2), (3))`
    `still open: the notice can still be given in time (s 72(2), (3))`
    `too late: the notice was not given in time (s 72(2), (3))`

-- The plaintiff's notice goes "when giving notice of trial": in time if given on the day notice of trial is given; still
-- open while notice of trial has not been given (fork F10).
GIVEN `I am entitled under s 72(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `side` IS A `My side`
      `notice of trial has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice of trial was given or received` IS A DATE
      `I have given the jury notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave the jury notice` IS A DATE
      `I have paid the jury fees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my jury on the re-hearing stands`
`s 72 -- where my jury on the re-hearing stands` `I am entitled under s 72(1)` `side` `notice of trial has been given` `the day notice of trial was given or received` `I have given the jury notice` `the day I gave the jury notice` `I have paid the jury fees` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT (`is a yes` `I am entitled under s 72(1)`)
    THEN `no jury as of right on the re-hearing (s 72(1))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the notice`
         WHEN `given in time` THEN
             IF `I have paid the jury fees`
             THEN `the jury notice is in time and the jury fees are paid: a jury of six (s 72)`
             ELSE `the jury notice is in time, but the jury fees are still to be paid (s 72(2), (3))`
         WHEN `still open` THEN `still open: the notice can still be given in time (s 72(2), (3))`
         WHEN `not given in time` THEN `too late: the notice was not given in time (s 72(2), (3))`
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS
            IF NOT `notice of trial has been given`
            THEN `still open`
            ELSE CONSIDER `side`
                 WHEN `the plaintiff` THEN
                     IF `I have given the jury notice`
                     THEN IF `the days from` `the day notice of trial was given or received` `to` `the day I gave the jury notice` EQUALS 0
                          THEN `given in time`
                          ELSE `not given in time`
                     ELSE `not given in time`
                 WHEN `the defendant side` THEN
                     `what became of the notice under` `s 72(3) -- the defendant's jury notice within four days` `given` `I have given the jury notice` `at` (`the days from` `the day notice of trial was given or received` `to` `the day I gave the jury notice`) `now` (`the days from` `the day notice of trial was given or received` `to` `today`)

§§ `Part VIII and Part II Division 7 -- enforcing the judgment (ss 49A(3), 86)`

-- s 86(1): "Whenever any judgment has been entered the registrar shall, upon application made by the judgment creditor ...,
-- grant and issue ... a certificate of such judgment and of the amount remaining due and unpaid thereon". (2): "No such
-- certificate shall be granted -- (a) before the expiration of any time during which execution could not be issued out of the
-- County Court; (b) if any warrant of execution has been issued out of the County Court under that judgment against the
-- person of the judgment debtor; or (c) until after the return of any warrant of execution issued out of the County Court
-- under that judgment against the goods and chattels of the judgment debtor." (3): after it issues, no further proceedings in
-- the County Court; (4): filed in the Supreme Court, final judgment there with interest at the penalty rate.
GIVEN `judgment has been entered for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time during which execution could not issue is still running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant has issued against the debtor's person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant against the debtor's goods has issued and not been returned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 -- I may have a certificate to take the judgment to the Supreme Court` `judgment has been entered for me` `a time during which execution could not issue is still running` `a warrant has issued against the debtor's person` `a warrant against the debtor's goods has issued and not been returned` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `judgment has been entered for me` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `a time during which execution could not issue is still running` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `a warrant has issued against the debtor's person` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `a warrant against the debtor's goods has issued and not been returned` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 49A(3): "Any person who dismisses an employee or injures him in his employment or alters his position to his prejudice by
-- reason of the circumstances that an attachment order has been made in relation to the earnings of that employee or that the
-- employee is required to make payments under such an order may be dealt with in the manner authorized by section 53 for
-- compelling obedience to or punishing disobedience of any judgment or order."
GIVEN `an attachment order has been made over my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer dismissed me, injured me in my employment or altered my position to my prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was because of the attachment order or the payments under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49A(3) -- my employer may be dealt with as for disobeying an order` `an attachment order has been made over my earnings` `my employer dismissed me, injured me in my employment or altered my position to my prejudice` `it was because of the attachment order or the payments under it` MEANS
    IF     `an attachment order has been made over my earnings`
       AND `my employer dismissed me, injured me in my employment or altered my position to my prejudice`
       AND `it was because of the attachment order or the payments under it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 49A(3) reaches only a prejudice "by reason of" the attachment order)

§§ `Part I Division 9 and Part VII -- costs and fees (ss 33, 34, 79A(6))`

-- s 33: "the costs of employing practitioners either by the plaintiff or defendant shall not be allowed as costs in the cause
-- in any civil case in which the amount recovered does not exceed $20 unless the court allows the same."
`s 33 -- the amount recovered at or below which practitioners' costs are not allowed` MEANS 20

GIVEN `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court allows the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33 -- my lawyer's costs may be allowed as costs in the cause` `the amount recovered` `the Court allows the costs` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the amount recovered` GREATER THAN `s 33 -- the amount recovered at or below which practitioners' costs are not allowed` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: above $20 s 33 bars nothing; costs are in the Court's discretion, s 78A(1))
           IF `the Court allows the costs` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 34(1): "The court may, upon the application of any person who has employed any legal practitioner in a proceeding, issue a
-- summons ... and ... the court shall proceed to assess the charges and fees of such practitioner for the proceeding."
-- (2): "If in the opinion of the court the charges or fees of such practitioner are unreasonable, it may, unless there is an
-- enforceable costs agreement under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria) to the contrary between the parties, order such
-- practitioner to repay any part of such charges or fees."
GIVEN `I employed the lawyer in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of opinion the charges are unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an enforceable costs agreement says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34 -- the Court may order my lawyer to repay charges` `I employed the lawyer in the proceeding` `the Court is of opinion the charges are unreasonable` `an enforceable costs agreement says otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I employed the lawyer in the proceeding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 34 is for the person who employed the practitioner)
           IF `an enforceable costs agreement says otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the Court is of opinion the charges are unreasonable` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 79A(6): "the registrar or a deputy registrar ... may, having regard to the income, day to day living expenses, liabilities
-- and assets of the person liable to pay a fee fixed under subsection (2)(a), waive payment of that fee if, in the registrar or
-- deputy registrar's opinion, the payment of that fee by that person would cause the person financial hardship and, in that
-- case, that fee is not payable." Subject to the fee regulations (not deposited).
GIVEN `the registrar is of opinion paying would cause me financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79A(6) -- the registrar may waive my court fee` `the registrar is of opinion paying would cause me financial hardship` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is of opinion paying would cause me financial hardship` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
